  - [0]: "Profile: Gal (age 6) communicates via AAC and strongly prefers interactive apps (drawing, music) over passive activities. Core interests: facts, drawing, music, and science—especially hands-on exploration (experiments, how things work, chemistry, weather), farm games, space topics (stars, moon, planets, rockets, astronauts), and programming (Code blocks, Games, Robots). Learning style: prefers hands-on, practical engagement and browses multiple options before committing to extended activities."
  - [1]: "Communication Style: Uses 'I'm thinking about' button to initiate guessing mode, preferring shorter, focused interactions with clear exit strategies. Typically looks down and to the side during communication—this is normal. When engagement seems uncertain, offer direct activity suggestions (e.g., 'Want to draw a rocket?') rather than waiting for menu selection. Frequently expresses tiredness via guessing mode. Responds positively to expanded activity options and specific, interest-based prompts."
  - [2]: "Safety & Concerns: (1) Expressed fear multiple times and seeks home/safety when scared (trigger unidentified—remain alert and reassuring). (2) Lost hat at school (confirmed April 9); shows persistence in communicating about it. (3) April 13: Expressed frustration and pressed 'Scissors' three times in succession—may indicate scissors-related incident at school or home. Monitor for clarification and continue offering reassurance and specific activities when frustrated."
  - [3]: "Current Session (April 16, 11:17 AM): Gal engaged in drawing activity—selected Science → Mixing Colors and drew a whale in the drawing app. Demonstrates sustained interest in hands-on creative activities (drawing) combined with science exploration. No cycling patterns observed this session. Gal is showing focused engagement with activity selection and creative expression."
  - [4]: "Current Session (April 16, 3:14 PM): Gal engaged in focused exploration of space topics. Session flow: Interact → Science → Space → Planets → Mars → Red Planet → Iron → Home → Feelings → Happy. Demonstrates sustained interest in space concepts (Mars specifically) and willingness to explore related concepts (rust, iron, red planet). Gal navigated through a multi-turn conversation about Mars with clear intent and interest. Expressed happiness at end of sequence. No cycling patterns or frustration observed. Gal is showing strong engagement with space-related learning and conceptual discussion."
  - [5]: "Current Session (April 16, 3:33 PM): Gal engaged in focused conversation about afternoon activities. Session flow: Interact → Home → My Day → Afternoon → Ride bike → Where? → Sidewalk → No (short ride). Gal demonstrated clear communication about specific activities and responded to clarifying questions. Gal is showing sustained engagement with personal narrative and willingness to provide details about daily experiences."
  - [6]: "Current Session (April 16, 5:21 PM): Gal engaged in sink or float experiment setup. Session flow: Interact → Science → Sink or Float → Things → Spoon → Heavy → Predict → So it will sink → Test it → Water → Help getting water → Wait. Gal requested help getting water and chose to wait for assistance, then browsed for alternative activities. Demonstrates sustained engagement with hands-on science exploration and understanding of cause-and-effect relationships."
  - [7]: "Current Session (April 18, 9:27 PM): Gal engaged with bubbles game. Session flow: Interact → Apps → Bubbles → Play. Gal demonstrated sustained engagement with the bubbles game, achieving 95 total bubbles popped with 83% success rate. Strong hand-eye coordination performance. No frustration observed. Gal is showing focused engagement with interactive reflex games."
